    "northStar": "Linuscent Aura reference library",
    "overview": "This is the established Linuscent Aura identity adapted to documentation, not a new identity. Near-black and navy surfaces, cyan interaction, geometric headings, and quiet reading text carry the parent brand without its cinematic decoration. A matching light theme uses darker cyan for legible interaction.\n\nThe implementation authority is `src/styles/theme.css` and `src/styles/docs.css`, with native Starlight components. Brand evidence comes from `../linuscent-website/src/styles/global.css`; it is not a runtime dependency. The official `public/logo-linuscent.png` remains unchanged, including its red color. This document describes implemented styling, not a browser-accessibility certification.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Cyan interaction with neutral reading surfaces.",
      "Self-hosted fonts and compact, flat components.",
      "Familiar Starlight navigation and search.",
      "Equivalent semantic roles in dark and light themes."
    ],
    "rules": [
      { "name": "The Semantic Color Rule", "body": "Consume `--aura-*` roles in shared CSS; never hard-code a theme's color into an article.", "section": "colors" }
